Subject: Cantor Self Work Update Broker B1 CDrive Production Preparation Operator Decision Verification P0 Dual Hemisphere Review

@ [review_uuid] 75006ea8-4238-4782-b115-94500d320074

& [Constructive]
  + a detached signature verifier is the smallest useful successor because the exact proposal object now exists and the production broker already expects a distinct operator authorization
  + embedding raw proposal bytes in the common request makes verification deterministic portable and independent of ambient repository state
  + signed authorize and reject outcomes give the operator one symmetric inspectable decision vocabulary without permitting either outcome to execute

& [Adversarial]
  + a valid signature under an arbitrary supplied key can be misread as governed consent unless policy_governance_proved and live_authorization_admitted remain false
  + temporal ordering can be misread as current validity unless ambient time is absent and current_nonexpired remains false
  + fixture keys and signatures can leak apparent authority unless fixture_only is transitive and no broker projection exists
  + raw proposal hash alone can hide semantic substitution unless UUID self-digest canonical parse implementation and bookend all validate

& [Synthesis]
  + admit cryptographic correspondence only and require separate policy governance external time fresh observation private permit and physical execution seams
